# fresh_dev_lifecycle_stop_reset_orders: stop and reset in both orders, then pause, stop while paused, and unpause: stop and reset are root-page writes of 0 (reset also zeroes the version, EFI and the device-info max key), and a second of either changes nothing once the root is gone (every register reads 0). The guest brings the device up again; stop while paused tears its root and display page down without dying, unpause raises one interrupt, and rvg_display_cursor_position then reads (0xffff, 0xffff).
